## v1.1.2b1

Changes since v1.1.0 (beta; includes the v1.1.1b1 preview fix):

+ Add persistent EOS usage and cleanup APIs backed by small REANA jobs, without
  requiring an EOS mount on the Yuki host. Isolate REANA SDK configuration in
  subprocesses and retain scan/plan IDs for recovery from uncertain submissions.
+ Classify measured caches as live, non-live or unknown using synchronized live
  sets and active workflow mirrors; report incomplete and unattributed entries.
+ Bind cleanup execution to a preview manifest and its SHA256. Revalidate scope,
  live classification, runner identity and filesystem metadata; block active
  project workflows and verify deletion in a separate REANA job.
  Report residuals as partial completion; never blindly resubmit deletions.
+ Fix `/remote-export` for native runner stageout files without prior collection.
  Preserve nested/repeated-task output paths, MIME detection, HEAD and HTTP byte
  ranges. Reject traversal and escaping symlinks; retain SSH/IHEP streaming.
+ Set Yuki to `1.1.2b1`. Upgrade Celebi and Yuki together for EOS commands and reload
  the Yuki HTTP service to register the new routes.

See docs/eos-usage.md and docs/release-1.1.2b1.md. This source beta does not itself
publish packages or remove any EOS data.
